Below is a practical, step‑by‑step guide you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for your e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole pipeline – from planning to deployment – and give you concrete choices, code snippets, and resources so you can start coding right away.

---

## 1️⃣ Planning & Design

| What | Why | How |
|------|-----|-----|
| **Define core features** | Product catalog, search, filters, product detail, cart, checkout, user account, reviews, admin panel | Write a feature list and prioritize |
| **Create user flows** | Understand how customers will navigate | Sketch flows in Figma/Adobe XD |
| **Wireframe / prototype** | Validate layout before coding | Use Figma, InVision, or Framer |
| **Design system** | Consistent UI components | Build a component library in Storybook + Figma |

> **Tip:** Keep the design system small at first – just the essentials (buttons, inputs, cards, modals). Expand later.

---

## 2️⃣ Choose a Tech Stack

| Category | Options | Recommendation |
|----------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular | **React** (most community, ecosystem) |
| **Language** | JavaScript, TypeScript | **TypeScript** (type safety, IDE support) |
| **State Management** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil | **Redux Toolkit** (simple, built‑in devtools) |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules, Styled‑Components, Tailwind CSS | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first, fast prototyping) |
| **Bundler** | Webpack, Vite, Parcel | **Vite** (fast dev server, ES modules) |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress | **Jest + RTL** for unit tests, **Cypress** for end‑to‑end |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI | **GitHub Actions** (free for public repos) |
| **Hosting** | Vercel, Netlify, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (automatic SSR, preview URLs) |
| **SSR / SSG** | Next.js, Nuxt.js, Remix | **Next.js** (React + SSR + SSG) |
| **API** | REST, GraphQL | **REST** (simpler for small projects) |
| **Auth** | Auth0, Firebase Auth, custom JWT | **Auth0** (quick login, social providers) |
| **Payments** | Stripe, PayPal, Braintree | **Stripe** (developer friendly, docs) |
| **Analytics** | Google Analytics, Plausible, Segment | **Google Analytics** (free, widely used) |

> **Why Next.js?** It gives you SSR/SSG out of the box, which is great for SEO and performance – both critical for e‑commerce.

---

## 3️⃣ Project Skeleton (Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind)

```bash
npx create-next-app@latest my-ecom --typescript
cd my-ecom
npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p
```

Add Tailwind config:

```js
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  content: [
    "./pages/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
    "./components/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
}
```

Add global styles:

```css
/* styles/globals.css */
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;
```

Now you have a ready‑to‑code environment.

---

## 4️⃣ Folder Structure

```
/my-ecom
├─ /components          # Reusable UI components
├─ /pages               # Next.js pages (routes)
├─ /public              # Static assets
├─ /styles              # Global CSS / Tailwind
├─ /hooks               # Custom hooks
├─ /utils               # Helper functions
├─ /services            # API calls
├─ /store               # Redux Toolkit slices
├─ /tests               # Jest + RTL tests
├─ /cypress             # Cypress e2e tests
└─ /config              # Environment variables
```

---

## 5️⃣ Core Pages & Components

### 5.1 Home Page (`pages/index.tsx`)

```tsx
import { GetStaticProps } from 'next';
import { fetchProducts } from '../services/api';

export default function Home({ products }) {
  return (
    <div className="container mx-auto p-4">
      <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Featured Products</h1>
      <ProductGrid products={products} />
    </div>
  );
}

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async () => {
  const products = await fetchProducts({ limit: 12 });
  return { props: { products }, revalidate: 60 };
};
```

### 5.2 Product Grid Component (`components/ProductGrid.tsx`)

```tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import Image from 'next/image';

export default function ProductGrid({ products }) {
  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
      {products.map((p) => (
        <Link key={p.id} href={`/product/${p.slug}`}>
          <a className="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
            <Image src={p.imageUrl} alt={p.title} width={300} height={300} objectFit="cover" />
            <div className="p-4">
              <h2 className="font-semibold">{p.title}</h2>
              <p className="text-gray-600">${p.price}</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        </Link>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 5.3 Product Detail Page (`pages/product/[slug].tsx`)

```tsx
import { GetStaticPaths, GetStaticProps } from 'next';
import { fetchProductBySlug, fetchAllSlugs } from '../../services/api';

export default function ProductDetail({ product }) {
  return (
    <div className="container mx-auto p-4 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8">
      <Image src={product.imageUrl} alt={product.title} width={500} height={500} />
      <div>
        <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold">{product.title}</h1>
        <p className="mt-2 text-xl text-gray-700">${product.price}</p>
        <p className="mt-4">{product.description}</p>
        <AddToCartButton productId={product.id} />
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

export const getStaticPaths: GetStaticPaths = async () => {
  const slugs = await fetchAllSlugs();
  return { paths: slugs.map((s) => ({ params: { slug: s } })), fallback: 'blocking' };
};

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async ({ params }) => {
  const product = await fetchProductBySlug(params.slug);
  return { props: { product }, revalidate: 60 };
};
```

### 5.4 Add to Cart Button (`components/AddToCartButton.tsx`)

```tsx
import { useDispatch } from 'react-redux';
import { addItem } from '../store/cartSlice';

export default function AddToCartButton({ productId }) {
  const dispatch = useDispatch();

  const handleClick = () => {
    dispatch(addItem({ id: productId, quantity: 1 }));
  };

  return (
    <button
      onClick={handleClick}
      className="mt-4 bg-blue-600 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded hover:bg-blue-700 transition"
    >
      Add to Cart
    </button>
  );
}
```

---

## 6️⃣ State Management (Redux Toolkit)

```bash
npm install @reduxjs/toolkit react-redux
```

Create a slice:

```ts
// store/cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

interface CartItem {
  id: string;
  quantity: number;
}

interface CartState {
  items: CartItem[];
}

const initialState: CartState = { items: [] };

export const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addItem(state, action: PayloadAction<CartItem>) {
      const existing = state.items.find((i) => i.id === action.payload.id);
      if (existing) {
        existing.quantity += action.payload.quantity;
      } else {
        state.items.push(action.payload);
      }
    },
    removeItem(state, action: PayloadAction<string>) {
      state.items = state.items.filter((i) => i.id !== action.payload);
    },
    clearCart(state) {
      state.items = [];
    },
  },
});

export const { addItem, removeItem, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

Configure store:

```ts
// store/store.ts
import { configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import cartReducer from './cartSlice';

export const store = configureStore({
  reducer: { cart: cartReducer },
});
```

Wrap app with provider:

```tsx
// pages/_app.tsx
import { Provider } from 'react-redux';
import { store } from '../store/store';
import '../styles/globals.css';

export default function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {
  return (
    <Provider store={store}>
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </Provider>
  );
}
```

---

## 7️⃣ API Layer

```ts
// services/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({ baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL });

export const fetchProducts = async (params) => {
  const { data } = await api.get('/products', { params });
  return data;
};

export const fetchProductBySlug = async (slug) => {
  const { data } = await api.get(`/products/${slug}`);
  return data;
};

export const fetchAllSlugs = async () => {
  const { data } = await api.get('/products/slugs');
  return data;
};
```

> **Tip:** Use environment variables (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`) for API endpoints.

---

## 8️⃣ Authentication (Auth0)

```bash
npm install @auth0/auth0-react
```

```tsx
// lib/auth0-provider.tsx
import { Auth0Provider } from '@auth0/auth0-react';
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';

export default function Auth0ProviderWithHistory({ children }) {
  const router = useRouter();

  const domain = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH0_DOMAIN;
  const clientId = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID;

  return (
    <Auth0Provider
      domain={domain}
      clientId={clientId}
      redirectUri={`${window.location.origin}${router.asPath}`}
    >
      {children}
    </Auth0Provider>
  );
}
```

Wrap app:

```tsx
// pages/_app.tsx
import Auth0ProviderWithHistory from '../lib/auth0-provider';

export default function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {
  return (
    <Auth0ProviderWithHistory>
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </Auth0ProviderWithHistory>
  );
}
```

Use hook:

```tsx
import { useAuth0 } from '@auth0/auth0-react';

const { loginWithRedirect, logout, user, isAuthenticated } = useAuth0();
```

---

## 9️⃣ Payment Integration (Stripe)

```bash
npm install stripe
```

Create a serverless function (Next.js API route):

```ts
// pages/api/checkout_sessions.ts
import Stripe from 'stripe';
const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, { apiVersion: '2023-10-16' });

export default async function handler(req, res) {
  if (req.method !== 'POST') return res.status(405).end();

  const { items } = req.body; // [{ priceId, quantity }]
  try {
    const session = await stripe.checkout.sessions.create({
      payment_method_types: ['card'],
      line_items: items.map((i) => ({
        price: i.priceId,
        quantity: i.quantity,
      })),
      mode: 'payment',
      success_url: `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/success`,
      cancel_url: `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/cancel`,
    });
    res.json({ sessionId: session.id });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
  }
}
```

Client side:

```tsx
import { loadStripe } from '@stripe/stripe-js';
const stripePromise = loadStripe(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY);

const handleCheckout = async () => {
